] [17592186436278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436260 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436262 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436263 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436264 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436270 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1077 "selection" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436260 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436278 1079 #uuid "a9112695-ad08-5300-a06c-ea0b770acb45" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436256 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436261 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436265 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436273 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436274 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1077 "selection" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436265 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436279 1079 #uuid "aded4a40-1d18-5fec-bc4b-4bcb36ab2d42" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436280 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436279 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436280 1069 "q-90448" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436280 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436280 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Give your answer rounded to two decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-1, & 2<x<3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{12}, & 3\\le x<4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436280 1072 #uuid "26e02fce-e08e-5fe6-a3ec-6ad998577401" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436280 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{5}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{5x}{12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})|}_{2}^{3}+{\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{24}|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}+\\frac{35}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{145}{48} \\\\  & ≈3.02,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nrounded to two decimal places." 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436281 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436276 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436281 1069 "q-131154" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436281 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436281 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2e-(e-1)X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{e}{e{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}},\\,1<x<e\n$$" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436281 1072 #uuid "3743ef7f-fa52-55af-8a67-99557ea6f27d" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436281 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2e-(e-1)X]=2e-(e-1)\\text{E}[X]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{e}{e{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{e}{ex-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{e-1}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{e}{e-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{e-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2e-(e-1)X] & =2e-(e-1)\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =2e-(e-1)\\cdot \\frac{e}{e-1} \\\\  & =2e-e \\\\  & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436282 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436277 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436282 1069 "q-152904" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436282 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436282 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[4X+2].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436282 1072 #uuid "c64c8376-4f9a-5df0-81b9-bf811d12f7ce" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436282 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of the expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[4X+2]=4\\text{E}[X]+2\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{2x})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{8}-0)+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4X+2] & =4\\text{E}[X]+2 \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{7}{8}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436283 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436278 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436283 1069 "q-152907" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436283 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436283 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[12X-8].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436283 1072 #uuid "edac9b93-8284-5302-bc8b-9583d4ecc8f3" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436283 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of the expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[12X-8]=12\\text{E}[X]-8\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{8}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8x}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12})|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{12}-0)+(\\frac{16}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[12X-8] & =12\\text{E}[X]-8 \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{17}{12}-8 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436284 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436285 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436284 1062 #uuid "07e26220-f667-5519-be8e-7ecfe5527804" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436284 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436280 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436285 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436288 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436285 1062 #uuid "4a878e04-e7e6-5c4d-a22c-de06d29307c3" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436285 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425379 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436286 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436287 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436286 1062 #uuid "5cb7073d-7ea9-5c29-94c4-88d377c15dab" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436286 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436282 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436287 1062 #uuid "95f58f9a-4473-5f86-8f32-f1873a14a714" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436287 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436283 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436288 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436286 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436288 1062 #uuid "d8cd80ec-e90e-5ae1-afb0-eecf1d561a37" 13194139534794 17592186045417 true] [17592186436288 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436281 13194139534794 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-ef1cf134-d58c-50a9-859d-b58621f65432" 17592186436255 "answer-01b4f1c9-6a5b-52c7-aa2b-f725b7d61594" 17592186436256 "answer-12065d32-e113-5992-bb8d-f535e75fb9ea" 17592186436257 "answer-18efb766-1d3d-58da-bff5-d24f02292777" 17592186436258 "answer-29173ece-c32d-5596-a3a8-34d0349c05ed" 17592186436259 "answer-30945d0b-c228-50cd-9399-4fc6759027b5" 17592186436260 "answer-3cd6386a-9b90-5c4e-be0a-bdee4537678d" 17592186436261 "answer-477a366f-5027-5734-8066-1c5b19a5ae4a" 17592186436262 "answer-52eacba8-2ac3-5a25-85fe-9c675a072c68" 17592186436263 "answer-5ffc82d5-d3b0-5643-